---
layout: base.njk
title: Hiking
description: Some of the hikes I've done over the years.
permalink: /hiking/
---
{% from "gallery.njk" import gallery %}

{% macro hikeEntry(hike) %}
  <article class="entry">
    <h3 class="entry__title">{{ hike.name }}</h3>
    <p class="entry__meta">{{ hike.date | longDate }} &middot; {{ hike.location }}</p>
    {{ hike.description | safe }}
    {{ gallery(hike.images, hike.name) }}
  </article>
{% endmacro %}

<h1>Hiking</h1>
<p class="hero__lede">{{ description }}</p>

<p>The one I still can't quite believe is Kilimanjaro: seven days up the Lemosho
route to 19,341 feet, the highest point on the African continent. Closer to home,
my sister and I spent a few weeks driving coast to coast across the northern US,
stopping at Maquoketa Caves, Badlands, Grand Teton, Yellowstone, Glacier and Mount
Rainier, then hiking in British Columbia before the drive back through Canada.</p>

<p>The long-running project is the 46ers, the Adirondack High Peaks over 4,000
feet. {{ outdoors.peaks.completed }} down, {{ outdoors.peaks.total - outdoors.peaks.completed }} to go.</p>

{% set shown = outdoors.hikes %}

{% for hike in shown.slice(0, 10) %}
  {{ hikeEntry(hike) }}
{% endfor %}

{% if shown.length > 10 %}
  <details class="disclosure">
    <summary>Earlier hikes ({{ shown.length - 10 }})</summary>
    {% for hike in shown.slice(10) %}
      {{ hikeEntry(hike) }}
    {% endfor %}
  </details>
{% endif %}
